  cat:source_ghsl_built_h schema:url <https://human-settlement.emergency.copernicus.eu/download.php?ds=builtH> .
  cat:source_ghsl_built_h schema:creditText "GHS-BUILT-H R2023A © European Union, 1995-2026, JRC (Pesaresi M., Politis P. (2023): GHS-BUILT-H R2023A - GHS building height, derived from AW3D30, SRTM30, and Sentinel2 composite (2018). European Commission, Joint Research Centre, doi:10.2905/85005901-3A49-48DD-9D19-6261354F56FE)" .
  cat:source_ghsl_built_h schema:publisher "European Commission, Joint Research Centre (JRC)" .
  cat:source_ghsl_built_h cat:registeredMetadata "{\"attribution\": \"GHS-BUILT-H R2023A © European Union, 1995-2026, JRC (Pesaresi M., Politis P. (2023): GHS-BUILT-H R2023A - GHS building height, derived from AW3D30, SRTM30, and Sentinel2 composite (2018). European Commission, Joint Research Centre, doi:10.2905/85005901-3A49-48DD-9D19-6261354F56FE)\", \"licence\": \"CC BY 4.0 (Commission reuse policy, Decision 2011/833/EU; copyright.txt in the GHS_BUILT_H_GLOBE_R2023A folder: \\\"(c) European Union, 1995-2026\\\")\", \"licence_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\", \"name\": \"GHS-BUILT-H R2023A: average net building height (ANBH), epoch 2018, 3 arc-second grid (EPSG:4326), 10 x 10 degree tiles (Global Human Settlement Layer)\", \"note\": \"Used for the places on the globe (adapter docklands/geo/adapters/world-ghsl.js, kind ghsl-raster): an OSM building with no height, no building:levels and no national floors takes the ANBH of the 3 arc-second cell under its centroid (a cell average, not a measure of the building). The 72 MB tile zip stays in cwplans/data/raw/places/<id>/ (git-ignored); the crop over each place is committed in cwplans/docklands/data/places/<id>/sources/ghsl-built-h.json (cropped and rounded to 0.1 m: a change, stated). Checked 2026-10-20: open download, no log-in. Also used for the German places (2026-10-22: berlin, stuttgart, dagstuhl; sets in danbri/docklandia data/de/).\", \"publisher\": \"European Commission, Joint Research Centre (JRC)\", \"url\": \"https://human-settlement.emergency.copernicus.eu/download.php?ds=builtH\"}" .
  cat:source_ghsl_built_h cat:recordStatus "Referenced source; distribution/harvest extent must be established from artifact and manifest links." .
  cat:source_overture_buildings a schema:Dataset .
  cat:source_overture_buildings schema:identifier "overture-buildings" .
  cat:source_overture_buildings schema:name "Overture Maps Foundation, buildings theme, release 2026-09-23.1 (GeoParquet on the public bucket overturemaps-us-west-2), read by bounding box with DuckDB" .
  cat:source_overture_buildings schema:description "Overture Maps Foundation, buildings theme, release 2026-09-23.1 (GeoParquet on the public bucket overturemaps-us-west-2), read by bounding box with DuckDB. Source listed by the project data register; listing alone does not prove acquisition or inclusion in all derived outputs." .
  cat:source_overture_buildings schema:includedInDataCatalog cat:catalogue .
  cat:source_overture_buildings dct:rights "ODbL 1.0 (buildings theme); per record and property the sources list names the original dataset and its licence" .
  cat:source_overture_buildings cat:recordedLicenceUrl <https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/> .
  cat:source_overture_buildings schema:license <https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/> .
  cat:source_overture_buildings schema:url <https://docs.overturemaps.org/attribution/> .
  cat:source_overture_buildings schema:creditText "© Overture Maps Foundation; © OpenStreetMap contributors; © Microsoft (and the other sources named per record)" .
  cat:source_overture_buildings schema:publisher "Overture Maps Foundation (records from OpenStreetMap, Microsoft ML Buildings, Instituto Geográfico Nacional (España), Esri Community Maps and others, named per record in its sources list)" .
  cat:source_overture_buildings cat:registeredMetadata "{\"attribution\": \"© Overture Maps Foundation; © OpenStreetMap contributors; © Microsoft (and the other sources named per record)\", \"licence\": \"ODbL 1.0 (buildings theme); per record and property the sources list names the original dataset and its licence\", \"licence_class\": \"share-alike\", \"licence_url\": \"https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/\", \"name\": \"Overture Maps Foundation, buildings theme, release 2026-09-23.1 (GeoParquet on the public bucket overturemaps-us-west-2), read by bounding box with DuckDB\", \"note\": \"Allowed by the owner on 2026-10-20 (\\\"Use ms/overture\\\"; CLAUDE.md, data policy). Used for the places on the globe (adapter docklands/geo/adapters/world-buildings.js, world-overture): heights, num_floors and roof_shape of records whose own source (the sources entry for that property) is not OpenStreetMap and whose source licence is open (ODbL, CDLA-Permissive, CC BY, CC0). Values with an empty licence field (León: 1,009 num_floors from Instituto Geográfico Nacional (España)) are neither used nor committed. The query answer stays in cwplans/data/raw/places/<id>/; only the crop of usable records is committed in places/<id>/sources/overture-buildings.json. Since 2026-10-20 also the buildings of the city box of each place (the city tier, place-select-outer): records whose geometry source is OpenStreetMap are drawn as blocks (OSM data); records from other sources give heights only (as in the core); the records whose geometry is from other datasets (León: IGN 10,858, Microsoft 1,909; Sarajevo: Microsoft 8,945) are counted and not drawn (the region config surround.geometry_sources can add them, with the owner's agreement). Also used for the German places (2026-10-22: berlin, stuttgart, dagstuhl; sets in danbri/docklandia data/de/).\", \"publisher\": \"Overture Maps Foundation (records from OpenStreetMap, Microsoft ML Buildings, Instituto Geográfico Nacional (España), Esri Community Maps and others, named per record in its sources list)\", \"url\": \"https://docs.overturemaps.org/attribution/\"}" .
  cat:source_overture_buildings cat:recordStatus "Referenced source; distribution/harvest extent must be established from artifact and manifest links." .
