  cat:source_overture_ign_floors schema:publisher "Instituto Geográfico Nacional (España), via the Overture Maps Foundation buildings theme" .
  cat:source_overture_ign_floors cat:registeredMetadata "{\"attribution\": \"Number of floors of some buildings from the Instituto Geográfico Nacional (España) via Overture Maps (licence not stated; kept apart, under review)\", \"licence\": \"not stated: the Overture sources entry of these records has an empty licence field (IGN data are generally CC BY 4.0; not confirmed for these records)\", \"licence_class\": \"review\", \"licence_url\": \"https://docs.overturemaps.org/attribution/\", \"name\": \"Overture Maps buildings, release 2026-09-23.1: the number of floors (num_floors) of the records whose source is \\\"Instituto Geográfico Nacional (España)\\\" (provider ign_es), over the León city box\", \"note\": \"These records are whole buildings whose geometry is from IGN (base source), not floors added to OSM buildings: they almost never overlap an OSM outline (1 of 9,782 matched), so as a height source they give 0 buildings; their value is the validation of F55 against the Catastro floors (curation skill, F55).\", \"publisher\": \"Instituto Geográfico Nacional (España), via the Overture Maps Foundation buildings theme\", \"review\": \"Owner, 2026-10-20: \\\"use the data but keep it distinct and easy to remove if requested. Use for validation at least\\\". Kept apart: adapter overture-ign-floors (docklands/geo/adapters/world-buildings.js), its own crop places/leon/sources/overture-ign-floors.json, its own height class \\\"overture-ign-floors\\\" after the national (Catastro) floors. Remove: delete the crop and the adapter id in place.heights of docklands/geo/regions/leon.js, then rebuild. Ask IGN / Overture for the licence of these records.\", \"review_exit\": \"catastro-ign\", \"url\": \"https://docs.overturemaps.org/attribution/\"}" .
  cat:source_overture_ign_floors cat:recordStatus "Referenced source; distribution/harvest extent must be established from artifact and manifest links." .
