  cat:artifact_242 cat:registeredMetadata "{\"osm\": {\"extract\": \"osmfr-greater-london\", \"use\": \"derived\", \"what\": \"the building outlines (through docklands/data/area.js: the minimum-area rectangle of each outline sets the ridge direction and spans) and the tags roof:shape, roof:height, roof:levels, roof:orientation of the buildings' OSM elements (osmium tags-filter on the extract of 2026-10-07)\"}, \"path\": \"docklands/data/roofs.json\", \"produced_by\": \"tools/build-roofs.mjs (operation build-roofs) with tools/lidar-roofs.py; tools/roofs-refine.mjs (operation roofs-refine)\", \"shown_on\": [\"docklands/index.html\"], \"sources\": [\"ea-lidar\", \"osm\", \"own\"], \"what\": \"roof shapes of the low model buildings of the 3D page (model height 25 m or less): gabled, hipped or pyramidal, with the ridge line (centre, bearing), half span, half ridge length, eave and ridge heights above the model ground; skillion roofs; an outline with wings (L, T, rear outriggers) cut into parts by chords from its reflex corners, a roof a part, with the run of a gable into a crossing wing (a valley); from robust plane fits to the EA LiDAR first-return DSM 2022 inside each outline or part, else from the OSM roof tags; the model fingerprint; counts by class and the OSM roof:shape against LiDAR class table; since 2026-10-22 (operation roofs-refine) the big buildings (footprint 4,000 m2 or more, any height) cut by roof level into flat parts (up to 24), and no LiDAR roof on a building newer than the survey\"}" .
