  cat:artifact_769 a schema:Dataset .
  cat:artifact_769 schema:name "docklands/data/places/sarajevo/tiles/*.glb" .
  cat:artifact_769 schema:description "Stari Grad, Sarajevo tiles (glTF 2.0 binary). Core, 15 level-15 cells: ground heightfield (copernicus-glo30, 32 x 32 cells, outer skirts) with a 512 px JPEG texture drawn from OSM water, green, squares, streets, rail and footprints; OSM buildings and building parts extruded from the lowest ground to mean ground + eaves height, with sloped roofs (gabled, hipped, pyramidal, skillion, dome) from OSM roof:shape or the region roof rule, else flat, vertex colours (OSM building:colour / roof:colour or defaults), _FEATURE_ID_0 = row of features.json (EXT_mesh_features); roofs: OSM roof:shape {\"pyramidal\": 24, \"gabled\": 38, \"hipped\": 4, \"skillion\": 44, \"dome\": 27}, region roof rule {\"hipped\": 6817}, flat 478 City and surroundings (place-lod, surroundings: 267 tiles, 7.31 MB; city: 132 tiles, 7.93 MB): a terrain grid (16 to 32 cells by level, normals from the DEM, skirts; KHR_mesh_quantization int16 positions, int8 normals, uint16 texture coordinates; the grid as a triangle strip) of the surroundings DEM (its outer 8 km eased to a 10 km box mean) with a 256 px JPEG texture painted from ESA WorldCover land cover, Overture water, rivers, roads by class and railways (OSM-derived), and the city building footprints; in the city box, OSM buildings as blocks (oriented boxes as EXT_mesh_gpu_instancing instances of one unit box, else simplified outlines; flat tops; heights by the place-heights order); since 2026-10-21 the city blocks also from Microsoft ML Buildings footprints (via Overture) where OSM has no building, each its own geometry class (switch in place.surround.geometry); glb extras.blocks: per block its class, height and height source (for the block card)" .
  cat:artifact_769 schema:includedInDataCatalog cat:catalogue .
  cat:artifact_769 cat:path "cwplans/docklands/data/places/sarajevo/tiles/*.glb" .
  cat:artifact_769 cat:registeredMetadata "{\"fetched\": \"2026-10-20\", \"note\": \"height_source \\\"ghsl\\\" (7,096 of 7,432 buildings and parts) = the GHS-BUILT-H R2023A average net building height of the 3 arc-second cell under the centroid (a cell average, CC BY 4.0); no Bosnia and Herzegovina national data used (FGU services need a log-in, a written request and a fee; owner waiver, issue https://github.com/danbri/londat/issues/9)\", \"osm\": {\"extract\": \"osm-api-place-sarajevo\", \"use\": \"derived\", \"what\": \"building outlines, parts, levels, roof tags, water, green, streets, rail (core, OSM API); roads, rail, water, building outlines and levels of the city and the surroundings (Overture release 2026-09-23.1, OSM-sourced records only, extract overture-osm-sarajevo)\"}, \"path\": \"docklands/data/places/sarajevo/tiles/*.glb\", \"produced_by\": \"tools/build-place-tiles.mjs\", \"shown_on\": [\"docklands/ (the Three.js port: the globe, globe/places.js)\"], \"sources\": [\"osm\", \"copernicus-glo30\", \"esa-worldcover\", \"overture-transportation\", \"overture-base\", \"overture-divisions\", \"ghsl-built-h\", \"overture-buildings\", \"ms-buildings\", \"own\", \"overture-ms-geometry\"], \"what\": \"Stari Grad, Sarajevo tiles (glTF 2.0 binary). Core, 15 level-15 cells: ground heightfield (copernicus-glo30, 32 x 32 cells, outer skirts) with a 512 px JPEG texture drawn from OSM water, green, squares, streets, rail and footprints; OSM buildings and building parts extruded from the lowest ground to mean ground + eaves height, with sloped roofs (gabled, hipped, pyramidal, skillion, dome) from OSM roof:shape or the region roof rule, else flat, vertex colours (OSM building:colour / roof:colour or defaults), _FEATURE_ID_0 = row of features.json (EXT_mesh_features); roofs: OSM roof:shape {\\\"pyramidal\\\": 24, \\\"gabled\\\": 38, \\\"hipped\\\": 4, \\\"skillion\\\": 44, \\\"dome\\\": 27}, region roof rule {\\\"hipped\\\": 6817}, flat 478 City and surroundings (place-lod, surroundings: 267 tiles, 7.31 MB; city: 132 tiles, 7.93 MB): a terrain grid (16 to 32 cells by level, normals from the DEM, skirts; KHR_mesh_quantization int16 positions, int8 normals, uint16 texture coordinates; the grid as a triangle strip) of the surroundings DEM (its outer 8 km eased to a 10 km box mean) with a 256 px JPEG texture painted from ESA WorldCover land cover, Overture water, rivers, roads by class and railways (OSM-derived), and the city building footprints; in the city box, OSM buildings as blocks (oriented boxes as EXT_mesh_gpu_instancing instances of one unit box, else simplified outlines; flat tops; heights by the place-heights order); since 2026-10-21 the city blocks also from Microsoft ML Buildings footprints (via Overture) where OSM has no building, each its own geometry class (switch in place.surround.geometry); glb extras.blocks: per block its class, height and height source (for the block card)\"}" .
