  cat:artifact_796 a schema:Dataset .
  cat:artifact_796 schema:name "docklands/data/places/london/tiles/*.glb" .
  cat:artifact_796 schema:description "Greater London block tiles (glTF 2.0 binary, one per quadtree cell with buildings; place-blocks 7 since 2026-10-23: far forms, issue #13, and the fill rule; the UK lite v2 way since 2026-10-22): at level 13 (leaves) every OSM building of 25 m2 or more and every Microsoft ML Buildings footprint (via Overture) of 25 m2 or more where OSM has none (class \"ms\") that is not named and not irregular, as one compact box (layout cwplans-boxes-1 in glb extras.blocks.compact: 8 bytes a box: its true centroid in the tile frame, footprint area, the angle and long / short ratio of its minimum rotated rectangle, height, height source, class; with a 17 x 17 ground grid); the irregular ones (300 m2 or more, filling less than 85 % of their oriented box: 63,607) as outlines simplified at 2.5 m (the place-blocks 3 rule, kept by architecture rule 6); and the named buildings (1,500 m2 or 20 m and more) as outlines with COLOR_0 and _FEATURE_ID_0 = row of features.json (EXT_mesh_features); at levels 10 to 12 the tall or big buildings as boxes (EXT_mesh_gpu_instancing) when they fill 0.7 of their oriented box, else as outlines simplified at 4 m (place-blocks 7), and the rest as far forms (compact kind blocks; no squares since place-blocks 6; street blocks cut until they fill 0.7): buildings and street blocks of adjacent buildings of similar height (oriented boxes within 5 m) at their true positions, one oriented box each with the summed footprint and the area-weighted mean height, drawn where their seen size sqrt(area) x max(sqrt(area), height) is at least 307 / 1,220 / 4,870 m2 (levels 12 / 11 / 10: about one device pixel squared at the far end of each level's range); flat tops; bases 3 m under the globe's ground (world-base GLO-90 heights + EGM96 geoid); KHR_mesh_quantization; glb extras.blocks: classes, height sources, the own boxes' class, height and source (block card), buildings of the cell" .
  cat:artifact_796 schema:includedInDataCatalog cat:catalogue .
  cat:artifact_796 cat:path "cwplans/docklands/data/places/london/tiles/*.glb" .
  cat:artifact_796 cat:registeredMetadata "{\"fetched\": \"2026-10-22\", \"osm\": {\"extract\": \"overture-osm-london\", \"use\": \"derived\", \"what\": \"building outlines, names, kinds, heights and levels of the OSM-sourced records of the Overture buildings theme (release 2026-09-23.1) inside the GLA boundary, outside the Docklands model box; Microsoft footprints only where no OSM outline overlaps them\"}, \"path\": \"docklands/data/places/london/tiles/*.glb\", \"produced_by\": \"tools/build-place-tiles.mjs\", \"review\": \"geometry class \\\"ms\\\" (349,432 blocks) = Microsoft ML Buildings footprints through Overture where OSM has none (ODbL, share-alike; owner 2026-10-22 \\\"yes\\\"; source overture-ms-geometry; switch place.blocks.geometry); height_source \\\"ms\\\" (566,358 buildings: 189,445 OSM outlines, 376,913 Microsoft outlines) = Microsoft ML Buildings heights through Overture (ODbL, share-alike; owner 2026-10-20 \\\"Use ms/overture\\\"); \\\"ghsl\\\" (713,191) = GHS-BUILT-H cell average (CC BY 4.0); \\\"osm-height\\\" 1,354, \\\"osm-levels\\\" 224,148 (ODbL); \\\"default-small\\\" 22,477 (3 m), \\\"default\\\" 149 (7 m)\", \"review_exit\": [\"osm-odbl\"], \"shown_on\": [\"docklands/ (the Three.js port: the globe, globe/places.js)\"], \"sources\": [\"osm\", \"overture-buildings\", \"ms-buildings\", \"overture-ms-geometry\", \"ghsl-built-h\", \"copernicus-glo90\", \"ons-boundaries\", \"own\"], \"what\": \"Greater London block tiles (glTF 2.0 binary, one per quadtree cell with buildings; place-blocks 7 since 2026-10-23: far forms, issue #13, and the fill rule; the UK lite v2 way since 2026-10-22): at level 13 (leaves) every OSM building of 25 m2 or more and every Microsoft ML Buildings footprint (via Overture) of 25 m2 or more where OSM has none (class \\\"ms\\\") that is not named and not irregular, as one compact box (layout cwplans-boxes-1 in glb extras.blocks.compact: 8 bytes a box: its true centroid in the tile frame, footprint area, the angle and long / short ratio of its minimum rotated rectangle, height, height source, class; with a 17 x 17 ground grid); the irregular ones (300 m2 or more, filling less than 85 % of their oriented box: 63,607) as outlines simplified at 2.5 m (the place-blocks 3 rule, kept by architecture rule 6); and the named buildings (1,500 m2 or 20 m and more) as outlines with COLOR_0 and _FEATURE_ID_0 = row of features.json (EXT_mesh_features); at levels 10 to 12 the tall or big buildings as boxes (EXT_mesh_gpu_instancing) when they fill 0.7 of their oriented box, else as outlines simplified at 4 m (place-blocks 7), and the rest as far forms (compact kind blocks; no squares since place-blocks 6; street blocks cut until they fill 0.7): buildings and street blocks of adjacent buildings of similar height (oriented boxes within 5 m) at their true positions, one oriented box each with the summed footprint and the area-weighted mean height, drawn where their seen size sqrt(area) x max(sqrt(area), height) is at least 307 / 1,220 / 4,870 m2 (levels 12 / 11 / 10: about one device pixel squared at the far end of each level's range); flat tops; bases 3 m under the globe's ground (world-base GLO-90 heights + EGM96 geoid); KHR_mesh_quantization; glb extras.blocks: classes, height sources, the own boxes' class, height and source (block card), buildings of the cell\"}" .
