  cat:branch_adsb_cache a schema:Dataset .
  cat:branch_adsb_cache schema:name "adsb-cache" .
  cat:branch_adsb_cache schema:description "Recorded aircraft tracks of the last 7 UTC days within 25 nm of 51.505 N 0.02 W (the 3D model box, the London City and Heathrow approaches), from the adsb.lol daily history: one gzip JSON file per UTC hour, legs with delta-coded points [t, lat, lon, altitude above the WGS84 ellipsoid, height source, ground speed, track], at most one point a second (one a minute above 15,000 ft); about 6 MB a day. Callsign only for operator ICAO callsigns without LADD/PIA flags; every other leg has an anonymous key and its type only; no ICAO address for those, and no registration, owner or squawk for any" .
  cat:branch_adsb_cache cat:registeredMetadata "{\"branch\": \"adsb-cache\", \"location\": \"https://github.com/danbri/londat/tree/adsb-cache (orphan branch, one commit, force-pushed by each run; the page reads it from https://raw.githubusercontent.com/danbri/londat/adsb-cache/)\", \"osm\": {\"use\": \"none\"}, \"paths\": [\"index.json\", \"README.md\", \"adsb/<YYYY-MM-DD>/day.json\", \"adsb/<YYYY-MM-DD>/<HH>.json.gz\"], \"produced_by\": \"tools/fetch-adsb-cache.mjs (workflow .github/workflows/adsb-cache.yml, daily; first backfill run by hand on 2026-10-09)\", \"review\": \"ODbL (share-alike) data committed to a branch (owner, 2026-10-09: \\\"For today build a cache of last 7 days for our areas, and show equivalent data for the matching time and day of week.\\\"). Review with the OSM (ODbL) use before anything leaves the prototyping phase; the owner's longer-term plan for live data is a proxy (\\\"Eventually find or build a proxy.\\\")\", \"review_exit\": \"adsb-odbl\", \"shown_on\": [\"docklands/ (the Three.js port, layer Aircraft)\"], \"sources\": [\"adsb-lol\"], \"what\": \"Recorded aircraft tracks of the last 7 UTC days within 25 nm of 51.505 N 0.02 W (the 3D model box, the London City and Heathrow approaches), from the adsb.lol daily history: one gzip JSON file per UTC hour, legs with delta-coded points [t, lat, lon, altitude above the WGS84 ellipsoid, height source, ground speed, track], at most one point a second (one a minute above 15,000 ft); about 6 MB a day. Callsign only for operator ICAO callsigns without LADD/PIA flags; every other leg has an anonymous key and its type only; no ICAO address for those, and no registration, owner or squawk for any\"}" .
  cat:branch_adsb_cache cat:sizeStatus "Not measured: separate branch not checked out; any sizes in description are register estimates." .
  cat:branch_adsb_cache cat:review "ODbL (share-alike) data committed to a branch (owner, 2026-10-09: \"For today build a cache of last 7 days for our areas, and show equivalent data for the matching time and day of week.\"). Review with the OSM (ODbL) use before anything leaves the prototyping phase; the owner's longer-term plan for live data is a proxy (\"Eventually find or build a proxy.\")" .
  cat:branch_adsb_cache schema:isBasedOn cat:source_adsb_lol .
  cat:branch_live_cache a schema:Dataset .
  cat:branch_live_cache schema:name "live-cache" .
  cat:branch_live_cache schema:description "Near-live data near now. aircraft.json: the adsb.lol live API answers of the last 60 minutes, 25 nm round 51.505 N 0.02 W, reports [t, lat, lon, altitude above the WGS84 ellipsoid, height source, ground speed, track, vertical rate, turn rate]; callsign and ICAO address only for operator ICAO callsigns without LADD/PIA flags, every other aircraft an anonymous key (joined by position) and its type only; no registration, owner or squawk. ships.json: Open Waters AIS vessels in 51.474-51.528 N, 0.095 W-0.085 E with their positions of the last 2 hours (the newest position of a listed vessel kept at any age), the licence filter of fetch-ais.mjs, small private craft counted only. metar.json: London City Airport METAR of the last 24 hours. metar-places.json (since 2026-10-22, issue #12): the METAR of the last 6 hours of the stations that the region configs name for the other places (about 48 stations). About 50 kB, 50 kB, 15 kB and 150 kB at steady state" .
  cat:branch_live_cache cat:registeredMetadata "{\"branch\": \"live-cache\", \"location\": \"https://github.com/danbri/londat/tree/live-cache (orphan branch, one commit, force-pushed every 5 minutes; the page reads it from https://raw.githubusercontent.com/danbri/londat/live-cache/)\", \"osm\": {\"use\": \"none\"}, \"paths\": [\"README.md\", \"aircraft.json\", \"ships.json\", \"metar.json\", \"metar-places.json\"], \"produced_by\": \"tools/fetch-live-cache.mjs (workflow .github/workflows/live-cache.yml, every 5 minutes; first runs by hand on 2026-10-09)\", \"review\": \"ODbL (adsb.lol) and scoping-only AIS (AISHub, aisstream.io) data committed to a branch (owner, 2026-10-09: \\\"Couldn't we crontab it for every 5 mins? And default to live for the rest?\\\", \\\"We want the webapp to always have fresh air and boat data plus recent history\\\", \\\"Basically we want all the data we can\\\"). Review with the OSM (ODbL) and AIS reviews before anything leaves the prototyping phase. The branch adsb-live was never created (the work moved to live-cache before the first push)\", \"review_exit\": [\"adsb-odbl\", \"ais-scoping\", \"metar-origin\"], \"shown_on\": [\"docklands/ (the Three.js port: layers Aircraft, Ships, Wind, Weather)\"], \"sources\": [\"adsb-lol\", \"openwaters-ais\", \"aishub-via-openwaters\", \"aisstream-via-openwaters\", \"openwaters-volunteer-cc0\", \"awc-metar\"], \"what\": \"Near-live data near now. aircraft.json: the adsb.lol live API answers of the last 60 minutes, 25 nm round 51.505 N 0.02 W, reports [t, lat, lon, altitude above the WGS84 ellipsoid, height source, ground speed, track, vertical rate, turn rate]; callsign and ICAO address only for operator ICAO callsigns without LADD/PIA flags, every other aircraft an anonymous key (joined by position) and its type only; no registration, owner or squawk. ships.json: Open Waters AIS vessels in 51.474-51.528 N, 0.095 W-0.085 E with their positions of the last 2 hours (the newest position of a listed vessel kept at any age), the licence filter of fetch-ais.mjs, small private craft counted only. metar.json: London City Airport METAR of the last 24 hours. metar-places.json (since 2026-10-22, issue #12): the METAR of the last 6 hours of the stations that the region configs name for the other places (about 48 stations). About 50 kB, 50 kB, 15 kB and 150 kB at steady state\"}" .
  cat:branch_live_cache cat:sizeStatus "Not measured: separate branch not checked out; any sizes in description are register estimates." .
  cat:branch_live_cache cat:review "ODbL (adsb.lol) and scoping-only AIS (AISHub, aisstream.io) data committed to a branch (owner, 2026-10-09: \"Couldn't we crontab it for every 5 mins? And default to live for the rest?\", \"We want the webapp to always have fresh air and boat data plus recent history\", \"Basically we want all the data we can\"). Review with the OSM (ODbL) and AIS reviews before anything leaves the prototyping phase. The branch adsb-live was never created (the work moved to live-cache before the first push)" .
  cat:branch_live_cache schema:isBasedOn cat:source_adsb_lol .
  cat:branch_live_cache schema:isBasedOn cat:source_openwaters_ais .
  cat:branch_live_cache schema:isBasedOn cat:source_aishub_via_openwaters .
  cat:branch_live_cache schema:isBasedOn cat:source_aisstream_via_openwaters .
  cat:branch_live_cache schema:isBasedOn cat:source_openwaters_volunteer_cc0 .
  cat:branch_live_cache schema:isBasedOn cat:source_awc_metar .
